 ## Background
-Random Pose Selection was proposed in the context of PeRFception, a method for perception using radiance fields [S1]. It addresses the issue of rendering failures when attempting to render extremely unobserved parts of a scene that are significantly out of train-view coverage [S1].
+Random Pose Selection was proposed in the context of PeRFception, a method for perception using radiance fields [S1]. It addresses the issue of rendering failures when attempting to render extremely unobserved parts of a scene that are significantly out of train-view coverage [S1]. The method is used within the PeRFception pipeline to generate training views for 3D ResUNets implemented with sparse convolutional layers on the PeRFception-ScanNet dataset [S1].
 
